 ('captive_wife_permitted', 'status', "the captive wife permitted — the STATUS the line captive_wife_declared writes on Israel: 'and you see among the captives a woman of beautiful form AND DESIRE HER AND TAKE HER FOR A WIFE' (21:11) — even a married woman, one not two; the Torah spoke against the evil inclination; the first act's permission disputed (the Sifrei 211:1-5, 212:1); taken_captive the tape's acts, references (midian by CALL)", H['captive'] + " (and desire her and take her for a wife — Deut 21:11)", "Deut 21:10-11, 20:1 (the opening's twin), Numbers 31:9 (midian by CALL), Genesis 29:17 (the phrase's kin); Onkelos 21:10-11; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 211:1-5, 212:1", CORPUS, EX % ("F6 the_captive — when_you_go_out_to_war_the_second, a_woman_of_beautiful_form", "captive_wife_declared")),
 ('captive_mourning_month_commanded', 'status', "the captive's mourning month commanded — the STATUS the line captive_wife_declared writes on Israel: 'she shall shave her head and do her nails and remove the garment of her captivity and sit in your house AND BEWAIL HER FATHER AND HER MOTHER A MONTH OF DAYS' (21:12-13) — the nails cut (R. Eliezer) or let grow (R. Akiva — Onkelos after him); her father and mother her idolatry (R. Akiva); thirty days (the Sifrei 212:2-4, 213:1-8); the month a parameter, no timer", H['month'] + " (and bewail her father and her mother a month of days — Deut 21:13)", "Deut 21:12-13, 2 Kings 15:13 (the phrase's other seat); Onkelos 21:12-13; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 212:2-4, 213:1-8", CORPUS, EX % ("F6 the_captive — the_head_the_nails_the_garment", "captive_wife_declared")),
 ('captive_sale_barred', 'block', "the captive's sale barred — the BLOCK the line captive_wife_declared writes on Israel: 'YOU SHALL SURELY NOT SELL HER FOR MONEY, you shall not deal with her as a slave, since you have humbled her' (21:14) — the doubled verb; Onkelos 'you shall not trade in her'; 'humbled' Hagar's word (primeval by CALL); the Sifrei 214:4-6, 215:1-3", H['sale'] + " (you shall surely not sell her for money — Deut 21:14)", "Deut 21:14, Genesis 16:6 (primeval by CALL), 2:5 (the trading verb's seats); Onkelos 21:14; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 214:4-6, 215:1-3", CORPUS, EX % ("F6 the_captive — if_you_delight_not_in_her", "captive_wife_declared")),
 ('captive_release_commanded', 'status', "the captive's release commanded — the STATUS the line captive_wife_declared writes on Israel: 'and if you delight not in her, YOU SHALL SEND HER AWAY FOR HERSELF' (21:14) — with a divorce document (the Sifrei 214:1-3 — 24:1's form; the release a divorce, the reading's crown)", H['release'] + " (you shall send her away for herself — Deut 21:14)", "Deut 21:14, 24:1; Onkelos 21:14; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 214:1-3", CORPUS, EX % ("F6 the_captive — if_you_delight_not_in_her", "captive_wife_declared")),
 ('firstborn_double_portion_commanded', 'status', "the firstborn's double portion commanded — the STATUS the line firstborn_portion_declared writes on Israel: 'the firstborn, the hated one's son, he shall acknowledge, TO GIVE HIM DOUBLE OF ALL THAT HE HAS, for he is the first of his strength' (21:17) — in the father's property, not the mother's, the held not the due (Mishnah Bekhorot 8:9 — the exam row); double of one share by 'of all that he has' and Jacob's one portion to Joseph (the Sifrei 217:2-8; family and zelophehad by CALL); 'the first of his strength' Reuben's (Genesis 49:3)", H['double'] + " (to give him double of all that he has — Deut 21:17)", "Deut 21:17, 17:6 (the consonants' homograph), Genesis 48:22, 49:3 (family by CALL), Numbers 27:8-11 (zelophehad by CALL), 1 Chronicles 5:1-2; Onkelos 21:17; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 217:2-8", CORPUS, EX % ("F7 the_firstborns_double — double_of_all_that_he_has", "firstborn_portion_declared")),
